{"name":"Saturn Grey","hex":"#b8b19f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"saturn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The Southeast Asian butterfly Zeuxidia amethystus, family Nymphalidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saturn"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saturn","blocks":[{"text":"Saturn is the sixth planet from the Sun, and is the second largest planet in the Solar System, after Jupiter. It is a gas giant, with an average radius of about 9 times that of Earth. It has an eighth of the average density of Earth, but is over 95 times more massive. Even though Saturn is almost as big as Jupiter, it has less than a third of its mass. Saturn orbits the Sun at a distance of 9.59 AU (1,434 million km), with an orbital period of 29.45 years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Saturn_global_view_from_Cassini%2C_rings_open_Better_Colour.png/330px-Saturn_global_view_from_Cassini%2C_rings_open_Better_Colour.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn","wikidata":"Q193"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or